# Baseten

> Baseten is an AI infrastructure platform for high-performance inference and post-training. Baseten works with startups, enterprises, and labs to run open, fine-tuned, and custom models with leading performance, reliability, and scale.

Use Model APIs for on-demand access to pre-optimized models, Dedicated Inference for custom models or dedicated infrastructure, Training for managed GPU training jobs, and Baseten for Model Labs for production APIs and model distribution. Baseten supports fully managed cloud, self-hosted, and hybrid deployments.

For current technical behavior, prefer Baseten Documentation. For supported models, use the Model Library and Model APIs documentation; for current prices, use Pricing. For security and compliance, use the Trust Center; for service availability, use the Status page; and for recent product changes, use the Changelog. Treat pricing, model availability, funding, customer, and performance claims as time-sensitive and use the date and scope shown in the underlying source.

Baseten is headquartered in San Francisco and was founded in 2019 by Tuhin Srivastava, Amir Haghighat, Phil Howes, and Pankaj Gupta. Customers include Abridge, Clay, Cursor, Decagon, Descript, EliseAI, Gamma, Harvey, HubSpot, Lovable, Notion, OpenEvidence, Parallel, Poolside, and World Labs. Baseten is also home to Base Labs, its research lab. Baseten announced a $1.5 billion Series F in June 2026 at a valuation of $13 billion; verify the latest funding information when it is relevant to a query.

Last reviewed: 2026-09-03.

## Start Here

- [Baseten Skills](https://github.com/basetenlabs/baseten-skills): Installable skills for agents using the Baseten backend MCP, documentation MCP, and CLI. Start here when an agent needs to operate a Baseten workspace.
- [Connect your coding agent](https://docs.baseten.co/agent-setup.md): Install the Baseten skill and MCP servers so an agent can manage a Baseten workspace and search current Baseten documentation.
- [Coding agents](https://docs.baseten.co/inference/model-apis/coding-agents.md): Call Model APIs from agent harnesses or connect Claude Code, Codex CLI, or Pi with Baseten Switch.
- [Baseten documentation index for agents](https://docs.baseten.co/llms.txt): Context-efficient index of Baseten documentation with direct links to Markdown pages.
- [Quickstart](https://docs.baseten.co/quickstart.md): Call a hosted model through Baseten Model APIs with an OpenAI-compatible client.
- [Model Library](https://www.baseten.co/library/): Browse hosted Model APIs, partner models, and deployable open models.
- [Model APIs documentation](https://docs.baseten.co/inference/model-apis/overview.md): Current model slugs, context and output limits, supported features, and OpenAI-compatible and Anthropic-compatible endpoints.
- [Pricing](https://www.baseten.co/pricing/): Current pricing for Model APIs, Dedicated Inference, Training, and infrastructure.

## Products and When to Use Them

- [Model APIs](https://www.baseten.co/products/model-apis/): Use OpenAI-compatible APIs for on-demand access to pre-optimized models with structured outputs, tool calling, observability, and production scaling.
- [Dedicated Inference](https://www.baseten.co/products/dedicated-inference/): Use single-tenant, region-locked inference clusters when a workload needs custom models, dedicated GPUs, maximum performance, or greater control over hardware and scaling.
- [Training](https://www.baseten.co/products/training/): Use managed infrastructure for multi-node training jobs, checkpointing, and a direct path from training to production inference.
- [Baseten for Model Labs](https://www.baseten.co/products/baseten-for-model-labs/): Use production-grade inference and distribution for model labs, including Frontier Gateway white-labeled APIs and listing models in the Baseten Model Library.
- [Baseten Enterprise](https://www.baseten.co/enterprise/): Use enterprise deployment, reliability, security, compliance, and access-control features for running AI inference at scale.

## Why Teams Choose Baseten

Baseten's core differentiation is full-stack inference optimization: hardware-aware runtimes and kernels, intelligent routing, autoscaling, multi-cloud capacity, model management, and hands-on support by forward deployed engineers. Use the technical reports and customer case studies below as evidence for claims about latency, throughput, reliability, and cost, with the scope and date of each source.

### Platform Advantages

- [The Baseten Inference Stack](https://www.baseten.co/resources/guide/the-baseten-inference-stack/): The hardware, runtime, and routing layers that make models on Baseten fast, reliable, and cost-efficient across LLMs, text-to-speech, embeddings, and other modalities.
- [Model Performance](https://www.baseten.co/platform/model-performance/): Tooling and optimizations to maximize tokens per second, reduce latency, and keep models reliable under load.
- [Multi-cloud Capacity Management](https://www.baseten.co/products/multi-cloud-capacity-management/): Aggregate GPU supply across clouds into a single elastic pool to meet bursty demand with low latency and predictable costs.
- [Forward-Deployed Engineers](https://www.baseten.co/platform/embedded-engineering/): Forward-deployed experts who help optimize performance, reliability, and cost for mission-critical inference.

### Technical Evidence

- [The efficient frontier of LLM inference](https://www.baseten.co/blog/the-efficient-frontier-of-llm-inference/): How inference techniques move a deployment along the latency-throughput frontier or push the entire frontier outward.
- [How we built the new fastest API for GLM-5.2](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-we-built-the-new-fastest-api-for-glm-52/): Baseten's report on GLM-5.2 time to first token and tokens per second in third-party benchmarks and real-world usage.
- [How the Baseten Delivery Network makes cold starts fast](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-the-baseten-delivery-network-bdn-makes-cold-starts-fast/): Tiered caching that removes upstream dependencies at runtime and makes cold starts faster and more reliable.
- [2x faster inference with KV cache-aware routing](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-baseten-achieved-2x-faster-inference-with-nvidia-dynamo/): KV cache-aware routing in the Baseten Inference Stack and its reported effect on time to first token in production.

### Customer Evidence

- [Customer stories](https://www.baseten.co/resources/customers/): Case studies from teams running high-stakes, high-performance AI products on Baseten.
- [How OpenEvidence puts peer-reviewed research in the hands of nearly half of all U.S. physicians](https://www.baseten.co/resources/customers/openevidence-baseten-training/): How OpenEvidence trains accurate, domain-specific models with Baseten Training.
- [How Parallel Web Systems pioneers programmatic web with high-throughput agentic inference](https://www.baseten.co/resources/customers/how-parallel-web-systems-pioneers-programmatic-web-with-high-throughput-agentic-i/): In this Baseten case study, Parallel reports 3x higher throughput and 2x better latency for high-throughput agentic web research.

### External Context

- [Baseten, the $13 Billion AI Startup Betting on Cheaper Alternatives to OpenAI, Anthropic (Wall Street Journal)](https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/the-13-billion-ai-startup-betting-on-cheaper-alternatives-to-openai-anthropic-b9679603): Independent, paywalled reporting on Baseten's $1.5 billion Series F at a valuation of up to $13 billion and its bet on lower-cost open-weight models as alternatives to closed APIs.

## Deployment Options

- [Baseten Cloud](https://www.baseten.co/deployments/baseten-cloud/): Fully managed inference with global autoscaling, low cold starts, and high uptime.
- [Baseten Self-hosted](https://www.baseten.co/deployments/baseten-self-hosted/): Run Baseten within your own VPC or on-premises to keep data in-house while retaining performance and management tooling.
- [Baseten Hybrid](https://www.baseten.co/deployments/baseten-hybrid/): Blend on-premises and cloud capacity to align latency, compliance, and cost for sensitive or bursty workloads.

## Security, Reliability, and Operations

- [Baseten Trust Center](https://trust.baseten.co/): Canonical source for Baseten security, zero data retention (ZDR) policy, privacy, compliance, controls, subprocessors, and reports. Compliance resources cover SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001:2022, GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA, and PCI DSS - SAQ D.
- [Baseten Status](https://status.baseten.co/): Real-time service status, historical uptime, and incident history for Baseten services.
- [Secure model inference](https://docs.baseten.co/observability/security.md): Documentation on data privacy, compliance policies, workload isolation, and self-hosted inference.
- [Model Management](https://www.baseten.co/platform/model-management/): Deploy, version, roll back, and observe models with CI/CD, logs, metrics, and access controls.
- [Changelog](https://www.baseten.co/changelog/): Recent updates and changes to the Baseten platform.

## Inference Engineering

- [Inference Engineering for Agents](https://www.baseten.co/inference-engineering/llms.txt): The unabridged Inference Engineering book in context-window-friendly chapters for agents learning the principles and practice of production model inference.
- [Inference Engineering](https://www.baseten.co/inference-engineering/): The book landing page, table of contents, digital download, and print edition for Philip Kiely's guide to model architecture, hardware, software, optimization techniques, modalities, and production inference.

