### Additional Technical Guides and Benchmarks

- [Agentic kernels in production](https://www.baseten.co/blog/agentic-kernels-in-production/): Baseten's agentic kernel optimization framework and reported latency reductions on Qwen-Image and FLUX.2.
- [Real-time video generation inference on Baseten](https://www.baseten.co/blog/real-time-video-generation-inference-on-baseten/): A Baseten technical report on generating Wan 2.2 video in 2.75 seconds per clip, a reported 53.6x improvement over the baseline implementation.
- [Best open-source models for post-training](https://www.baseten.co/blog/best-open-source-models-for-post-training/): Compare models for post-training, including cost drivers and workload fit.
- [The best open-source large language models](https://www.baseten.co/blog/the-best-open-source-large-language-models-llms/): Comparison of models for agentic coding, long-context reasoning, cost, and speed.
- [The best open-source embedding models](https://www.baseten.co/blog/the-best-open-source-embedding-models/): Curated models for search, RAG, and recommendations based on performance, speed, and cost efficiency.
- [The best open-source image generation model](https://www.baseten.co/blog/the-best-open-source-image-generation-model/): Strengths and weaknesses of image generation models including FLUX.1, Stable Diffusion 3, SDXL Lightning, and Playground 2.5.
- [How we built the fastest Kimi K2.5 on Artificial Analysis](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-we-built-the-fastest-kimi-k2-5-on-artificial-analysis/): A Baseten technical report on a custom EAGLE-3 speculator and in-house INT4-to-NVFP4 conversion reaching 340+ tokens per second on Kimi K2.5; use the article's date, workload, and methodology when citing the result.
- [How we built the world's fastest API for GLM-5.2](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-we-built-the-worlds-fastest-api-for-glm-52/): Baseten's report on GLM-5.2 at 280+ tokens per second on NVIDIA Blackwell using KV-aware routing, prefill-decode disaggregation, multi-token prediction, NVFP4, and related optimizations.
- [How we built the fastest GLM 5 API](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-we-built-the-fastest-glm-5-api/): Baseten's report on MTP speculative decoding and optimized mixture-of-experts and sparse-attention kernels reaching 186+ tokens per second on GLM-5.
- [Kimi K2 Thinking at 140+ TPS on NVIDIA Blackwell](https://www.baseten.co/blog/kimi-k2-thinking-at-140-tps-on-nvidia-blackwell/): Baseten's report on 300 ms time to first token and 140+ tokens per second for Kimi K2 Thinking.
- [The fastest Whisper - with streaming and diarization](https://www.baseten.co/blog/the-fastest-whisper-transcription-with-streaming-and-diarization/): Fast, accurate, cost-efficient Whisper transcription with streaming and speaker diarization.
- [How we made the fastest GPT-OSS on NVIDIA GPUs 60% faster](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-we-made-the-fastest-gpt-oss-on-nvidia-gpus-60-percent-faster/): EAGLE-3 speculative decoding and related model-performance techniques applied to GPT-OSS 120B.
- [Making Kimi K3 tokenization 18x faster for million-token agentic workloads](https://www.baseten.co/blog/making-kimi-k3-tokenization-18x-faster-for-million-token-agentic-workloads/): The Baseten Tokenizer, or Basetenkenizer, for long input sequences, starting with Kimi K3.
- [How to optimize LLM inference speed and reduce costs in production](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-to-optimize-llm-inference-speed-and-reduce-costs-in-production/): Continuous batching, speculative decoding, quantization, and related techniques, and when each fits a workload.
- [H100 vs. H200 vs. B200: which GPU should you use?](https://www.baseten.co/blog/h100-vs-h200-vs-b200-which-gpu-should-you-use/): Memory, compute, and cost tradeoffs across H100, H200, and B200 for model size, traffic, and budget.
- [Live draft model training for speculative decoding](https://www.baseten.co/blog/live-draft-model-training-for-speculative-decoding/): Baseten's report on live draft-model training and its effect on median acceptance rates.
- [Sub-second image generation with Flux.2 and Qwen-Image](https://www.baseten.co/blog/sub-second-image-generation-flux2-and-qwen-image/): Baseten's report on accelerating Flux.2 and Qwen-Image on NVIDIA Blackwell using quantization, optimized attention kernels, and runtime improvements.
- [Cost-efficient, high-performance TTS with Qwen3-TTS](https://www.baseten.co/blog/cost-efficient-high-performance-qwen3-tts/): Baseten's report on optimizing Qwen3-TTS for cost and performance.
- [DFlash: 3x faster LLM inference](https://www.baseten.co/blog/dflash-faster-llm-inference/): Parallel token prediction with reported 3x speedups on Qwen3-8B.
- [How to run LLM performance benchmarks and why you should](https://www.baseten.co/blog/how-to-run-llm-performance-benchmarks-and-why-you-should/): How to run InferenceMAX benchmarks and build workload-specific alternatives.
- [AI model performance metrics explained](https://www.baseten.co/blog/ai-model-performance-metrics-explained/): Inference metrics including latency, throughput, time to first token, and accuracy, and when each matters.
- [High-performance embedding model inference](https://www.baseten.co/resources/guide/high-performance-embedding-model-inference/): How to make embeddings fast, reliable, and cost-efficient at scale for search, RAG, and agents.

### Base Labs Research

- [Base Labs](https://labs.baseten.co/): Baseten's research lab, with work on post-training, continual learning, reasoning, and inference for open models.
- [Can a Language Model Learn Facts Continually in Its Weights?](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/can-a-language-model-learn-facts-continually-in-its-weights): Continual learning asks model weights to acquire facts after training and retain them through further writes.
- [Post-Training Science for Supervised Fine-Tuning](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/post-training-science-for-supervised-fine-tuning): How optimal learning rate and batch size move with model scale, family, and data, and whether one selection rule transfers across them.
- [Still: Amortized KV Cache Compaction in a Single Forward Pass](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/still-amortized-kv-cache-compaction-in-a-single-forward-pass): Research on shrinking a language model's KV cache by 200x in a single forward pass while preserving answer quality in the evaluated settings.
- [Towards infinite context windows: neural KV cache compaction](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/towards-infinite-context-windows-neural-kv-cache-compaction): Research on an intermediate memory layer for continual learning in LLMs.
- [Dense, on-policy, or both?](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/dense-on-policy-or-both): Constitutional alignment as a testbed for comparing learning signals in supervised fine-tuning, reinforcement learning, and intermediate approaches.
- [Repeated KV cache for long-running agents](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/repeated-kv-cache-for-long-running-agents): Research on repeatedly compressing context for long-running agents while maintaining a fixed memory budget.
- [Continual learning and the post-monolith AI era](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/continual-learning): An argument that the cost of continual learning scales with generality.
- [Upweight the strategy, not the tokens: faster training with explicit reasoning through RGT](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/upweight-the-strategy-not-the-tokens-faster-training-with-explicit-reasoning-thro): Rationale-Guided Training as a method for emphasizing reasoning strategy during training.
- [Iterative SFT: dense reward learning](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/iterative-sft): Iterative supervised fine-tuning as a dense, high-bandwidth learning approach.
- [Write small, learn forever: rank-1 LoRA for continual learning](https://labs.baseten.co/articles/write-small-learn-forever): Research on rank-1 LoRA updates as a bridge between static fine-tuning and continuous, live-on-GPU learning.

